@startuml documents
title Document scenarios
autonumber
actor "User" as User
participant "hermes (CLI / TUI)" as Client
participant "hermes-document-service" as HDS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Create a document ==
User -> Client : Create document (workspace_id, title, Markdown)
Client -> HDS : CreateDocument(..., session)
alt Workspace unavailable or role below editor
  HDS --> Client : Denied; no changes
else Access allowed
  group Single transaction
    HDS -> DB : Check membership and non-empty title
    HDS -> DB : Create document with version=1 and author attribution
    HDS -> DB : Outbox: DocumentCreated
  end
  HDS --> Client : Document and version
end
note over HDS
  Personal documents belong to the personal workspace.
  DocumentCreated does not notify all workspace members.
end note

== List and search documents ==
User -> Client : List or search available documents
Client -> HDS : ListDocuments / SearchDocuments(workspace_id?, query, cursor)
HDS -> DB : Select active documents in accessible workspaces only
HDS --> Client : IDs, titles and next cursor
Client --> User : Show results

== Read and edit a document ==
User -> Client : Read or edit document
Client -> HDS : GetDocument(id, session)
HDS -> DB : Validate membership and active document
HDS --> Client : title, content, version or unavailable
opt Edit an accessible document
  Client -> Client : Keep original version; open external editor
  User -> Client : Finish editing
  Client -> Client : Read changes and keep local recovery copy
  Client -> HDS : UpdateDocument(id, title, content, expected_version)
  group Single transaction
    HDS -> DB : Check edit permission, document status and expected_version
    alt Permission lost or document unavailable
      HDS --> Client : Access error; no changes
    else Version mismatch
      HDS --> Client : Conflict; no changes
    else Matching version and changed content
      HDS -> DB : Update document and increment version
      HDS -> DB : Outbox: DocumentUpdated
      HDS --> Client : Saved; new version after commit
    else Matching version and unchanged content
      HDS --> Client : Current version; no update event
    end
  end
  alt Save succeeded
    Client --> User : Show saved or unchanged result
  else Conflict, access error or network failure
    Client --> User : Show error and path to local recovery copy
    opt User chooses conflict resolution
      Client -> HDS : GetDocument(id, session)
      HDS --> Client : Latest version if still accessible
      Client --> User : Offer manual comparison and another edit
    end
  end
end
note over Client
  TUI refreshes the inbox after the editor exits.
  An unknown network outcome is checked by reading the document.
  Never overwrite a newer version without checking it.
end note

== Subscribe or unsubscribe ==
User -> Client : Subscribe to document changes or unsubscribe
Client -> HDS : SubscribeDocument / UnsubscribeDocument
HDS -> DB : Transaction: check access; update subscription;\noutbox DocumentSubscriptionCreated/Deleted only if changed
HDS --> Client : Current subscription state
note over HDS, DB
  Subscription grants no access and is removed when access is lost.
  Repeating the same state does not create another event.
end note

== Delete a document ==
User -> Client : Delete document
Client -> HDS : GetDocument(id, session)
HDS --> Client : Document and version after access check
Client --> User : Request deletion confirmation
User -> Client : Confirm
Client -> HDS : DeleteDocument(id, expected_version, confirmation)
group Single transaction
  HDS -> DB : Check editor/admin/owner, active status and version
  alt Checks passed
    HDS -> DB : Capture subscriber IDs; soft-delete document
    HDS -> DB : Remove subscriptions
    HDS -> DB : Outbox: DocumentDeleted with subscriber IDs
  else Access denied, deleted document or stale version
    HDS -> DB : No changes
  end
end
HDS --> Client : Deleted, unavailable or conflict
Client --> User : Show result
note over HDS
  DocumentDeleted sends subscribers with current membership a minimal notice.
  The deleted document cannot be opened.
  Other notifications targeting the inaccessible document are hidden.
end note
@enduml
